/-!
# The structure sheaf of the small étale site of an algebraic space (Stacks 03G6)

Let `S` be a scheme in a big fppf site `B` and let `F` be an algebraic space over `S`. The
rule sending an étale scheme chart `U` of `F` to the ring `Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` of its global regular
functions is a sheaf of rings on the small étale site of `F`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structurePresheaf` is the presheaf of commutative rings
  of global regular functions on the étale scheme charts of `F`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.structureSheaf` packages it with its sheaf condition.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.structurePresheaf_isSheaf` — **Stacks 03G6**: that
  presheaf is a sheaf for the small étale topology of `F`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.isEtaleChart_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.hasPullbacks` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.preservesPullbacks_toScheme`: the small étale site of an
  algebraic space has fibre products and they are the fibre products of the underlying schemes.
* `Stacks.Sites.isContinuous_of_precoverage_le`: a general site lemma deriving continuity of a
  functor from a single inequality of precoverages.

## Implementation notes

**Stacks 03G6 lives in Chapter 66**, *Properties of Algebraic Spaces*. Only Stacks 03G6 is
proved here; nothing is newly *defined* that belongs to Chapter 66, every notion used being
already available, namely `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEtaleChart` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale`.

**Stacks 03G6 is registered elsewhere in the library**, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structurePresheaf_isSheaf`, together with the continuity statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.isContinuous_toScheme`, the covering comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.precoverage_le_comap_fpqcTopology` and the reflection
lemma `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_commRingCat_of_isSheaf_forget`.  This file imports rather than
restates them; the imported continuity statement carries no algebraicity hypothesis.  What
remains here is the small étale site's own
`structurePresheaf`, `structurePresheaf_isSheaf` and `structureSheaf`, which live in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale` namespace and are what the atlas development consumes.

**The route is not the source's.** Stacks 03G6 cites Descent, Lemma 03DT; another possible
route goes through the slice category `Over S`, a comparison of `Scheme.Γ` with
the functor represented by `Spec`, and a polynomial-generator argument that recovers elements
of a ring from ring maps out of `ℤ[X]`. Neither is used. This library already has the
fpqc sheaf of global sections on *all* schemes,
`Stacks.Sites.globalSectionsSheaf`, together with
`Stacks.Sites.globalSectionsSheaf_obj` identifying its underlying presheaf of types with
`Scheme.Γ ⋙ forget CommRingCat`, so the whole content reduces to continuity of the functor
from the small étale site of `F` to all schemes. That is why a Chapter-66 tag is reached by a
Chapter-59 theorem: a `proof_uses` entry is a fact about the source's proof, not about this
one, and Stacks 03DT is used nowhere here.

**Continuity needs only fibre products, not a base-change-stable precoverage.**
`Stacks.Sites.isContinuous_of_precoverage_le` derives continuity of `G` for the topology
generated by a precoverage `J` from the single inequality `J ≤ K.toPrecoverage.comap G`; the
stability and pullback hypotheses that Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_toGrothendieck_of_pullbacksPreservedBy` wants are
inherited by the comparison precoverage `K.toPrecoverage.comap G` from the target topology
`K`, so `J` itself needs none of them. All that is left is fibre products in the source and
the target and their preservation, which is why
`isEtaleChart_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan` is the only geometric input: a fibre
product of two étale charts of `F` is again one, because its projection to the first chart is
a base change of an étale morphism of charts (Stacks 03EC, `morphism_between_charts`) and
composing with an étale chart is étale (Stacks 03EC, `composition`).

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.precoverage_le_comap_fpqcTopology` carries **no**
algebraicity hypothesis, and that is not an oversight: a covering family of the small étale
site of an arbitrary presheaf is by definition one whose underlying family of schemes is a
selected étale covering, so it is an fpqc covering whatever `F` is. Algebraicity enters only
through the fibre products.

`structureSheaf` has no consumer in this library yet. It is retained rather than removed
because it is the object the source's sentence is about and the entry point the Stacks 0DMY
ring of global functions is the sections of; that is a disclosure, not a claim of use.

The presheaf is valued in `CommRingCat` rather than `RingCat`, which is what the source means
by a sheaf of rings on a scheme-theoretic site and what every consumer of this sheaf needs.
Since `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_ringCat_of_isSheaf_forget` is stated for `RingCat`, the
commutative analogue `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_commRingCat_of_isSheaf_forget` is used instead; it
reflects the limit of the sieve diagram along `forget CommRingCat`, where Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_forget` does not apply, because it asks the
coefficient category to be a `Category.{max u v}` and `CommRingCat.{u}` is a `Category.{u}`.

Only `structurePresheaf_isSheaf` carries the tag. The source asserts one thing — that the rule
`U ↦ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` is a sheaf — so that theorem is the whole covering set; the presheaf and the
bundled sheaf are *Main definitions*, naming the object the assertion is about, and are left
untagged.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G6)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe v u v' u'

namespace Stacks.Sites

/-- A functor into a site is continuous for a topology generated by a precoverage as soon as
that precoverage refines the comparison precoverage `K.toPrecoverage.comap G`. The source and
the target need fibre products and `G` must preserve them, but the precoverage itself needs no
stability hypothesis: the comparison precoverage inherits all of them from `K`. -/
theorem isContinuous_of_precoverage_le
    {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D]
    [HasPullbacks C] [HasPullbacks D]
    (J : Precoverage C) (K : GrothendieckTopology D) (G : C ⥤ D)
    [PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan G]
    (hJ : J ≤ K.toPrecoverage.comap G) : G.IsContinuous J.toGrothendieck K := by
  refine ⟨fun P => (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).mp ?_⟩
  have := Functor.isContinuous_toGrothendieck_of_pullbacksPreservedBy G
    (K.toPrecoverage.comap G) K.toPrecoverage le_rfl
  exact Presheaf.IsSheaf.of_le (Precoverage.toGrothendieck_mono hJ)
    (G.op_comp_isSheaf_of_isSheaf _ K.toPrecoverage.toGrothendieck P.obj
      (Presheaf.IsSheaf.of_le (GrothendieckTopology.toGrothendieck_toPrecoverage_le K)
        P.property))

end Stacks.Sites

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)

/-- A fibre product of two étale charts of an algebraic space is again an étale chart: the
projection to the first factor is a base change of an étale morphism between charts, and an
étale morphism of schemes followed by an étale chart is an étale chart. -/
theorem isEtaleChart_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan
    (_hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F) :
    (IsEtaleChart B S hS F).IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan := by
  set P := IsEtaleChart B S hS F with hP
  set G := BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS with hG
  let _ : P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms := by
    let _ : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        G).presheaf.RespectsIso :=
      MorphismProperty.relative_respectsIso _
    rw [hP]
    change ((MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      G).presheaf.costructuredArrowObj yoneda (X := F)).IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms
    infer_instance
  set K := CostructuredArrow.proj (yoneda : BigFppfOver B S hS ⥤ _) F ⋙ G with hK
  let _ : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan G := by
    rw [hG]; apply comp_preservesLimitsOfShape
  let _ : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan K := by
    rw [hK]; apply comp_preservesLimitsOfShape
  apply ObjectProperty.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape.mk'
  rintro X ⟨D, hD⟩
  have hpb : IsPullback (G.map (limit.π D WalkingCospan.left).left)
      (G.map (limit.π D WalkingCospan.right).left)
      (G.map (D.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inl).left)
      (G.map (D.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inr).left) :=
    IsPullback.of_isLimit_cone (isLimitOfPreserves K (limit.isLimit D))
  have hr : Etale (G.map (D.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inr).left) :=
    etale_of_etale_charts B S hS
      (D.obj WalkingCospan.right).hom (D.obj WalkingCospan.one).hom
      (hD WalkingCospan.right) (hD WalkingCospan.one)
      (D.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inr).left (D.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inr).w
  have hpl : Etale (G.map (limit.π D WalkingCospan.left).left) :=
    MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange.of_isPullback hpb.flip hr
  rw [hP]
  change (MorphismProperty.presheaf
    (MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) G))
    (limit D).hom
  rw [show (limit D).hom =
      yoneda.map (limit.π D WalkingCospan.left).left ≫ (D.obj WalkingCospan.left).hom by
    simp]
  exact etale_comp_of_scheme B S hS (limit.π D WalkingCospan.left).left
    (D.obj WalkingCospan.left).hom hpl (hD WalkingCospan.left)

/-- The small étale site of an algebraic space has fibre products. -/
theorem hasPullbacks (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F) :
    HasPullbacks (SmallEtale B S hS F) := by
  let _ := isEtaleChart_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan B S hS F hF
  change HasPullbacks (IsEtaleChart B S hS F).FullSubcategory
  infer_instance

/-- The fibre products of the small étale site of an algebraic space are the fibre products of
the underlying schemes. -/
theorem preservesPullbacks_toScheme (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F) :
    PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan
      (toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) := by
  let _ := isEtaleChart_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan B S hS F hF
  let _ : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (inclusion B S hS F) := by
    change PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (IsEtaleChart B S hS F).ι
    infer_instance
  apply comp_preservesLimitsOfShape

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale

end
